# Compiled WebAssembly build output for crates/kotva-sync-wasm (`build.sh`). These are BUILD OUTPUT.
# Carried over with the crate when it moved here from envoir, along with the reasoning: committing
# a wasm blob once cost a real bug (a stale checked-in module kept aborting on free long after the
# source had been fixed), because nothing in git ties a binary to the code that produced it.
crates/kotva-sync-wasm/pkg/
crates/kotva-sync-wasm/pkg-node/
crates/kotva-sync-wasm/pkg-web/
# NOT ignored, deliberately: bindings/go/kotva_sync_abi.wasm. A Go module has no build step, so
# gitignoring it makes the package uncompilable for anyone who `go get`s it. That artifact buys the
# guarantee back explicitly instead — wasm_provenance.json + provenance_test.go fail when it drifts
# from its source. See bindings/go/embed.go.
